## 3. Nucleus v0.3.0: V2 Task Orchestration System

**Date:** 2026-01-03

### Summary

After **14 exhaustive thinking passes** covering mechanisms, CS theory, philosophy, history, and operations, implemented the complete V2 Task Orchestration System for Nucleus.

### What Was Built

**6 New MCP Tools:**
| Tool | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- |
| [brain_list_tasks](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#567-586) | Query tasks with filters (status, priority, skill, claimed_by) |
| [brain_get_next_task](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#587-598) | Pull highest-priority unblocked task matching agent skills |
| [brain_claim_task](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#599-611) | Atomically claim a task (prevents race conditions) |
| [brain_update_task](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#612-624) | Modify task fields (status, priority, etc.) |
| [brain_add_task](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#625-646) | Create new tasks with full V2 schema |
| [brain_escalate](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#647-659) | Request human help when stuck |

**11-Field Task Schema:**
```
id, description, status, priority, blocked_by, required_skills,
claimed_by, source, escalation_reason, created_at, updated_at
```

**Status States:** `PENDING | READY | IN_PROGRESS | BLOCKED | DONE | FAILED | ESCALATED`

### Test Coverage

- **44 tests passed** (all passing)
- **66% code coverage** on main module
- Unit tests for all 6 tools
- Integration tests for full task lifecycle
- Edge case coverage: already claimed, nonexistent, legacy format
- Safety property tests: referential integrity, DAG validation

